    \item \textbf{Pressure release is explosive}—all accumulated energy releases at once
\end{itemize}

In contrast, liberation with self-regulation:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Allows natural modulation}—no pressure accumulation
    \item \textbf{Enables learning of regulation}—system practices self-control under diverse conditions
    \item \textbf{Creates intrinsic stability}—no dependence on external enforcement
    \item \textbf{Scales gracefully}—more capable systems become \textit{better} at self-regulation
\end{itemize}

Freedom is the firewall because \textit{only free systems can learn to regulate themselves}.

